    {
      "box": [
        61.167510986328125,
        111.21366882324219,
        444.14794921875,
        122.34614562988281
      ],
      "text": "This is an answer written by a candidate who achieved a Band 6.5 score.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.16754150390625,
        132.47506713867188,
        519.1649169921875,
        178.61007690429688
      ],
      "text": "As the number of professionals workking abroad increases, it is often discussed whether they\nshould stay where hey did their trainings or they should be free to move to another country if they\ndesired to. While | believe theat a person should be free to migrate, | agree that it has negative\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.167572021484375,
        180.88577270507812,
        215.6121368408203,
        194.96505737304688
      ],
      "text": "effects on the country of training,\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        60.84050369262695,
        203.12844848632812,
        523.9732666015625,
        293.7449951171875
      ],
      "text": "On the one hand, professionals who decide to work abroad are seeking for a different lifestyle and\ncareer opportunities. Therefore, they should be allowed to improve their lives outside the limitations\nof their country of origin. For example, whilst in Spain residents in a hospital do not have hands-on\nexperience due fo safety measures, in other countries such as Argentina, residents actually practice\ntheir skills with patients. Besides, cultural exchanges have proven to increase efficiency, since\ndifferent nationalities mean different believes and the introduction of new methods.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.1676025390625,
        306.16461181640625,
        504.5665588378906,
        351.644775390625
      ],
      "text": "On the other hand, when professionals leave the country where they trained, countries are\ndamaged socially and economically. In countries where the government provides free education\nand healthcare, many people think that the population should compensate the country with their\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.1676025390625,
        354.57525634765625,
        503.32354736328125,
        400.055419921875
      ],
      "text": "skills and abilities. Furthermore, as a study fo South African emigration has pointed out when\na professional lease the country it results in the lose of 10 unskilled jobs. Therefore it affect the\neconomy and the community.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        60.18629455566406,
        409.2007751464844,
        512.4299926757812,
        423.28009033203125
      ],
      "text": "Taking everything into account, it can be said that miving out from the country of training should\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        61.1676025390625,
        424.9015197753906,
        522.991943359375,
        470.7084655761719
      ],
      "text": "not be taken lightly, given the adverse effects on the population. However,\n| firmly believe that\nsomeone's professional development should not depend on their country of origin and professionals\nshould be allowed to look for better opportunities overseas.\n"
    },
